This product is designed to use the following third-party models and tools on the deploy box.
Each is used under its own license; see the model cards and repositories for the exact terms.

NVIDIA open models (NVIDIA Open Model License / CC-BY-4.0 / OpenMDW-1.1 as noted on each card):
  - nvidia/nemotron-speech-streaming-en-0.6b   (streaming ASR)
  - nvidia/magpie_tts_multilingual_357m         (TTS)
  - nvidia/Nemotron-3_5-Lightning               (live replies, via Nebius Token Factory)
  - nvidia/nemotron-3-super-120b-a12b           (nightly hints/plan/card, via Token Factory)
  - nvidia/parakeet_realtime_eou_120m-v1        (end-of-utterance signal; controller input only)
  - nvidia/NVIDIA-NemotronLabs-VoiceChat-11B    (recorded baseline in the video only; license
                                                 OpenMDW-1.1 on Hugging Face)

Frameworks and libraries (Apache-2.0 / BSD / MIT / ISC as noted in pyproject.toml):
  - pipecat-ai, silero-vad, nemo_toolkit, torch
  - openai (client to Token Factory), tenacity, instructor
  - rapidfuzz, jellyfish, nltk (CMUdict), epitran, fsrs
  - fastapi, uvicorn, pydantic, pydantic-settings
  - sqlalchemy, asyncpg, aiosqlite, alembic, saq
  - numpy, soundfile, librosa, pyloudnorm, soxr, audiotsm
  - structlog, opentelemetry-sdk, arize-phoenix
  - NVIDIA NemoClaw, NVIDIA OpenShell, Nous Research Hermes Agent (carer channel)

No AphasiaBank audio or any real patient data is included in this repository. Demo speech is
synthetic or recorded by consenting volunteers reading a script.

Read each license file before distributing.
